## Media index DB (MediaDbContext) schema & relationships

DbContext:
- `src/Bible.Alarm.Shared/Database/MediaDbContext.cs`

### Tables (high-signal)

- `Languages`
  - `LanguageCode` is unique (also enforced by EF)
  - includes text direction (`ltr`/`rtl`)

- `Categories`
  - logical grouping: “Bible”, “Music”, “Dramas”, “Video”

- `BaseUrls` (+ `UrlParams`)
  - URL construction metadata used to build JW API URLs

- `UrlParams`
  - **Only tracks store UrlParams** - complete params needed to fetch that specific track
  - `UrlParams.BiblePublicationTrackId` → `BiblePublicationTracks.Id`
  - Each track's `UrlParams` contains all parameters needed to construct the full download URL (e.g., `pub`, `booknum`, `fileformat`, `langwritten`, `track`, `alllangs`)
  - **Sections and Publications do NOT store UrlParams** - URLs are built in code using harvest-type logic (see `FlatPublicationFetcher.cs`, `SectionFetcher.cs`)

- `BiblePublications`
  - `CategoryId` required
  - `LanguageId` optional:
    - **null LanguageId** = “no-language” publications (not language-specific), e.g. melody music

- `BiblePublicationSections`
  - optional depending on publication type
  - cascade delete from `BiblePublications`

- `BiblePublicationTracks`
  - tracks can be:
    - sectioned (linked to `BiblePublicationSections`)
    - flat (section FK null)

