## Media DB “shape matrix” (publication ↔ language ↔ sections)

The Media DB supports a few **independent axes**. Most bugs in cascade/playback/url generation come from assuming one axis implies another.

### Axes (the 3 possibilities you called out)

- **PublicationCode always exists**
  - `BiblePublications.PublicationCode` is the stable identifier (“nwt”, “iam”, “sjj”, etc.)
- **Language can exist / not exist**
  - `BiblePublications.LanguageId != null`: language-bound publication (normal case)
  - `BiblePublications.LanguageId == null`: “no-language” publication (shared across languages), e.g. melody releases
- **Sections can exist / not exist**
  - sectioned: `BiblePublicationSections` rows exist and tracks may have `BiblePublicationSectionId != null`
  - non-sectioned (flat): no sections; tracks have `BiblePublicationSectionId == null`

### Practical combinations we support

- **Language-bound + Sectioned**
  - typical Bible pattern: Publication → Sections → Tracks
  - selection keys: `(LanguageCode, PublicationCode, SectionCode, TrackCode)`
- **Language-bound + Flat**
  - typical vocal music / many videos: Publication → Tracks
  - selection keys: `(LanguageCode, PublicationCode, TrackCode)` (no SectionCode)
- **No-language + Sectioned**
  - melody discs (e.g. `iam`): Publication → Sections (disc codes) → Tracks
  - selection keys: `(PublicationCode, SectionCode, TrackCode)` (no LanguageCode)
- **No-language + Flat**
  - less common, but structurally supported: Publication → Tracks (no LanguageCode, no SectionCode)

- `PublicationLanguages` (discovery table)
  - “catalog” of which languages exist per publication
  - `LanguageId` can be null for “no-language” availability rows
  - includes optional `HarvestType` override (Flat / Sectioned / MediatorSectioned)

- `SectionLanguages` (discovery table)
  - “catalog” of which languages exist per section of a publication
  - required `PublicationLanguageId` → enforces “section implies publication exists”

### Relationship sketch

```text
Category (1) ──< BiblePublications (many)
Category (1) ──< PublicationLanguages (many)

Language (1) ──< BiblePublications (many)        [optional FK]
Language (1) ──< PublicationLanguages (many)     [optional FK]
Language (1) ──< SectionLanguages (many)         [optional FK]

BiblePublications (1) ──< BiblePublicationSections (many)  [cascade]
BiblePublications (1) ──< BiblePublicationTracks (many)    [cascade]

BiblePublicationSections (1) ──< BiblePublicationTracks (many) [optional section FK]

PublicationLanguages (1) ──< SectionLanguages (many) [cascade]
```

### How categories are used (media DB)

Categories are used to:
- filter the language list by category (`PublicationLanguages` drives “languages available in this category”)
- filter publications by category (e.g. “Music” schedules vs “Bible” schedules)
- support “no-language” category publications (notably **instrumental music**) via `BiblePublications.LanguageId == null`

The schedule UI category selection and cascade logic depends on category strings matching the DB’s `Category.CategoryName` (e.g. `"Music"`).

