## Schedule DB (ScheduleDbContext) schema & relationships

DbContext:
- `src/Bible.Alarm.Shared/Database/ScheduleDbContext.cs`

### Tables (high-signal)

- `AlarmSchedules`
  - core schedule definition: time, days-of-week, enabled flags
  - alarm options: snooze, number of tracks, always-play-from-start
  - `CronExpression` is derived and used to compute next fire time (Quartz)

- `BiblePublicationSchedules` (1:1 with `AlarmSchedules`)
  - the main “what to play” pointer:
    - `LanguageCode`
    - `PublicationCode`
    - optional `SectionCode`
    - `TrackCode`
    - `FinishedDuration`

- `AlarmMusic` (1:1 with `AlarmSchedules`)
  - “begin with music” configuration (pre-roll music)
  - has `MusicType` (instrumental vs vocal), and can also be sectioned (disc/section)
  - code notes label it as “obsolete/backward compatibility” but it’s still used for begin-with-music

- `AlarmNotifications`
  - tracks OS-level scheduling metadata per schedule

- `GeneralSettings`
  - key/value settings (`AppConstants.GeneralSettingsKeys.*`)

### Schedule DB relationships

- `AlarmSchedule` ↔ `BiblePublicationSchedule` is **one-to-one** (cascade delete)
- `AlarmSchedule` ↔ `AlarmMusic` is **one-to-one** (cascade delete)
- `AlarmSchedule` ↔ `AlarmNotifications` is **one-to-many**

